        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): retry reply session init conflicts to prevent silent message loss",
        "body": "Closes #102381\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Discord inbound messages could be silently dropped when a reply session initialization conflict (`reply session initialization conflicted for <sessionKey>`) raced with another turn finishing or another event initializing the same session. Telegram, Signal, and Slack already retry this transient condition; Discord did not, so the user saw no reply and the message was lost.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded bounded exponential backoff retry inside `processDiscordMessageInner` (`extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.process.ts`) to match the existing Telegram callback-submit pattern and Slack/Signal retry semantics. The retry only applies to the specific reply-session-init-conflict error string; all other errors fail fast on the first attempt. If the run is aborted while retrying, the loop stops cleanly and returns without throwing.\n\n**ClawSweeper review follow-up:** the retry boundary was narrowed so context/history preparation runs exactly once and only the dispatch/session-init attempt is retried. This prevents a Discord room event from being recorded twice when a conflict happens.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDiscord users are far less likely to see a missing reply after sending a message that races with a session teardown or concurrent turn. Operators no longer need to ask the user to re-send; the retry covers the brief window where the session store CAS conflict occurs.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added a focused regression test suite in `extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.process.test.ts`:\n  - retries with exponential backoff until dispatch succeeds (250 ms, 1000 ms, 2500 ms)\n  - throws the last error after exhausting retries\n  - does not retry unrelated dispatch errors\n  - stops retrying when the abort signal fires\n  - **records room event history exactly once across conflict retries** (new regression test for the narrowed boundary)\n- Full local focused run:\n  - `npx vitest run extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.process.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-discord.config.ts` → 120 passed\n  - `npx vitest run extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.queue.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-discord.config.ts` → 22 passed\n  - `npx vitest run extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.process.test.ts extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.process.abort-skip.test.ts extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.queue.test.ts extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-handler.preflight.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-discord.config.ts` → 198 passed\n- `oxlint` and `oxfmt` clean on changed files.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nThis environment does not have the `crabbox` binary or a live Discord bot token, so a redacted live Discord conflict-to-success trace cannot be generated locally. Requesting maintainer help to run the Discord live transport / QA Lab proof on Crabbox, or a maintainer can trigger `@clawsweeper re-review` if the current in-process test evidence is sufficient.",
